From: LookBack <admin@dstw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PHP7.2 GHSA-www2-q4fc-65wf: reject NUL in dns_get_record/dns_get_mx on Linux

Supplement to security/3125-network-nul-parameters.patch (left unchanged for
traceability). The PHP 7.2 version of 3125 converted dns_check_record in
ext/standard/dns.c, but dns_get_record and dns_get_mx were only converted in
the Windows implementation ext/standard/dns_win32.c; the Linux implementation
in ext/standard/dns.c still used Z_PARAM_STRING and accepted hostnames with
embedded NUL bytes (truncated lookups). This switches both to Z_PARAM_PATH,
line-for-line identical to the corresponding php-7.3.33 ext/standard/dns.c
code in this project. Regression: ext/standard/tests/network/ghsa-www2-q4fc-65wf.phpt
(all 9 "valid path" warnings).

--- a/ext/standard/dns.c
+++ b/ext/standard/dns.c
@@ -815,7 +815,7 @@
 	zend_bool raw = 0;
 
 	ZEND_PARSE_PARAMETERS_START(1, 5)
-		Z_PARAM_STRING(hostname, hostname_len)
+		Z_PARAM_PATH(hostname, hostname_len)
 		Z_PARAM_OPTIONAL
 		Z_PARAM_LONG(type_param)
 		Z_PARAM_ZVAL_DEREF_EX(authns, 1, 0)
@@ -1050,7 +1050,7 @@
 #endif
 
 	ZEND_PARSE_PARAMETERS_START(2, 3)
-		Z_PARAM_STRING(hostname, hostname_len)
+		Z_PARAM_PATH(hostname, hostname_len)
 		Z_PARAM_ZVAL_DEREF(mx_list)
 		Z_PARAM_OPTIONAL
 		Z_PARAM_ZVAL_DEREF(weight_list)
